        "hash": "a60a173503d1a36e5c80f936a268a329fd142f00",
        "subject": "Stop the FAB speed-dial label clipping off the left edge",
        "body": "Stop the FAB speed-dial label clipping off the left edge\n\nReported on a real iPhone 15 Pro and logged in PHASE_STATUS.md, but never\nfixed. Rows are right-anchored at screenWidth/2 + MINI_SIZE/2 and grow\nleftward, and the label has flexShrink: 0, so anything wider than the left\nhalf of the screen minus the mini FAB runs off-screen rather than wrapping.\n\n\"Subir estado de cuenta\" needs roughly 169pt at Inter 13 SemiBold. A 393pt\niPhone 15 Pro leaves 162pt, so it clipped; a 402pt iPhone 17 Pro leaves 167pt,\nso it did not — which is why the simulator hid this.\n\nCap the label at a width derived from the screen so the text wraps instead.\nShortening the string would have been fragile: Spanish is the primary locale\nand Dynamic Type can still overflow any fixed copy.\n\nVerified on the simulator with real iOS text metrics: the label now wraps to\ntwo lines and sits fully on screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
        "author": {
          "name": "Nived Vengilat",
          "email": "nivedvengilat@gmail.com",
          "time": 1787099357000
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Nived Vengilat",
          "email": "nivedvengilat@gmail.com",
          "time": 1787099357000
        },
